      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're highlighting a key point. Without a global framework, companies are indeed likely to take advantage of weaker regulations in various countries, creating uneven playing fields. This can lead to a \"race to the bottom,\" where countries compete to offer the most favorable conditions for corporate investment, at the expense of worker rights, environmental protection, and public well-being. Cooperation and unified standards, like those proposed by the Trans-Pacific Green Alliance, can help mitigate this risk, promoting a more level playing field and incentivizing countries to adopt more stringent standards.",
